Step 0 has already exposed the key track constraint: the paper itself gives a randomized efficient algorithm for finding the minor model in its promised expander regime. That rules out an honest Track A claim. I’m now checking whether there is a genuine Track B compression gap—large mechanical search versus a short structural recovery route—or whether the only plausible planting would make the model visibly easy and force rejection.
