The long pole is the exact G8 check, not generation or grading: it is recomputing relabelling-invariant distance/4-cycle profiles across 40 medium-size graph encodings. The process is healthy; once it completes I’ll trim that invariant if it is needlessly expensive, while keeping the required 20-seed proof.
 succeeded in 79608ms:
